  "question": {
    "text": "Mean of 5 observations is 7 . If four of these observations are $6,7,8,10$ and one is missing then the variance of all the five observations is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9LL2s",
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GA5VZ",
      "text": "\n6\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l2dJI",
      "text": "\n8\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WTZ7C",
      "text": "\n2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let 5 th observation be $x$.\nGiven mean $=7$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore 7=\\frac{6+7+8+10+x}{5} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow x=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nNow, Variance\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n=\\sqrt{\\frac{(6-7)^2+(7-7)^2+(8-7)^2+(10-7)^2+(4-7)^2}{5}} \\\\\n=\\sqrt{\\frac{1^2+0^2+1^2+3^2+3^2}{5}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{20}{5}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\n\\end{gathered}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
